### CreditDesk API — manual requests
### Open in VS Code / Codespaces with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request" above each block.
### Start the stack first: `docker compose up --build` (repository root). Demo users: infra/keycloak/README.md.
###
### Run the 4 login requests first: the others reuse their tokens ({{ana.response.body.access_token}} etc.).
### Tokens last 5 minutes — when you get a 401, just send the login again.

@base = http://localhost:8080
@token_url = http://localhost:8180/realms/creditdesk/protocol/openid-connect/token

### ── Login (password grant: local development only) ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# @name ana
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=creditdesk-cli&username=ana&password=ana-demo

###
# @name bruno
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=creditdesk-cli&username=bruno&password=bruno-demo

###
# @name marcos
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=creditdesk-cli&username=marcos&password=marcos-demo

###
# @name aline
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=creditdesk-cli&username=aline&password=aline-demo

### ── Security basics ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### No token → 401 problem + WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
GET {{base}}/api/customers

### Auditor trying to write → 403
POST {{base}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{aline.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "PF", "document": "529.982.247-25", "name": "Not Allowed", "email": "x@example.com", "monthlyRevenue": 1 }

### ── Customers (analyst) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Search customers (CPF comes back masked; the database only has it encrypted)
GET {{base}}/api/customers?size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}

### Search by document — works through the HMAC hash, without decrypting anything
GET {{base}}/api/customers?document=41.395.376/0001-20
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}

### Register an individual (PF) — the CPF below is a generated test number
# @name newCustomer
POST {{base}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: requests-http-0001

{
  "type": "PF",
  "document": "529.982.247-25",
  "name": "Maria da Silva",
  "email": "maria.silva@example.com",
  "monthlyRevenue": 8500.00
}

### Same document again → 409 duplicate-document
POST {{base}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "PF", "document": "52998224725", "name": "Maria Duplicada", "email": "dup@example.com", "monthlyRevenue": 100 }

### Read it: the response carries ETag: "0"
GET {{base}}/api/customers/{{newCustomer.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}

### Update WITHOUT If-Match → 428 precondition-required
PUT {{base}}/api/customers/{{newCustomer.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Maria da Silva Souza", "email": "maria.souza@example.com", "monthlyRevenue": 9200.00 }

### Update with the version you read → 200, ETag: "1". Send it twice: the second one is 412 (stale)
PUT {{base}}/api/customers/{{newCustomer.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "0"
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Maria da Silva Souza", "email": "maria.souza@example.com", "monthlyRevenue": 9200.00 }

### ── Proposal workflow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Ana creates a proposal (DRAFT, owned by ana, ETag "0")
# @name newProposal
POST {{base}}/api/proposals
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{newCustomer.response.body.id}}",
  "kind": "NEW_CREDIT",
  "amount": 15000.00,
  "installments": 24,
  "monthlyRate": 0.0199
}

### Bruno tries to submit Ana's proposal → 403 not-proposal-owner
POST {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "0"

### Ana submits → SUBMITTED, ETag "1"
POST {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "0"

### Ana tries to start the analysis → 403 (analysts cannot decide proposals)
POST {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}/start-analysis
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "1"

### Marcos (manager) picks it up → IN_ANALYSIS, ETag "2"
POST {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}/start-analysis
Authorization: Bearer {{marcos.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "1"

### Approve with a stale version → 412 (it is "2" now)
POST {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{marcos.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "1"

### Return to the analyst (reason required) → DRAFT again, editable, ETag "3"
POST {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}/return
Authorization: Bearer {{marcos.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "2"
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Missing proof of income" }

### Ana edits the returned draft
PUT {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "3"
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "NEW_CREDIT", "amount": 12000.00, "installments": 24, "monthlyRate": 0.0199 }

### Timeline: who moved it, when and why
GET {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}

### Only my proposals
GET {{base}}/api/proposals?mine=true
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}

### Approve from DRAFT → 422 invalid-transition
POST {{base}}/api/proposals/{{newProposal.response.body.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{marcos.response.body.access_token}}
If-Match: "4"

### Filter by status and period (max 90 days)
GET {{base}}/api/proposals?status=APPROVED&size=50
Authorization: Bearer {{marcos.response.body.access_token}}

### ── Audit (manager, auditor) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Everything that happened to the proposal above
GET {{base}}/api/audit?entityType=PROPOSAL&entityId={{newProposal.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aline.response.body.access_token}}

### Analysts cannot read the audit trail → 403
GET {{base}}/api/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{ana.response.body.access_token}}

### Auditor reveals the full CPF — reason mandatory, and the reveal itself is audited
POST {{base}}/api/customers/{{newCustomer.response.body.id}}/document/reveal
Authorization: Bearer {{aline.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Ticket SAC-0042: confirm customer identity" }

### …and here it is in the trail, with the reason and the correlation id
GET {{base}}/api/audit?entityId={{newCustomer.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aline.response.body.access_token}}

### Health probes used by Kubernetes (public)
GET {{base}}/actuator/health/readiness
